    "intro": "Common e-bike issues and how to resolve them — troubleshooting guides from the shop.",
    "articles": [
      {
        "id": "stops-suddenly",
        "title": "What to do if the E-Bike suddenly stop",
        "html": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"></span><strong style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-size: 14px;\">What to do if the E-Bike suddenly stop</strong></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-align: justify;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:12pt;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 12px; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\">What to do if the unit suddenly stop while driving? Here are the possible reasons:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-indent: 36pt;text-align: justify;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:12pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">1</span><span style=\"font-size: 12px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; There are wires that are cut loose</span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-indent: 36pt;text-align: justify;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:12pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">2.</span><span style=\"font-size: 12px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; There’s a problem with Motor and/or Control Panel</span></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;text-indent: 36pt;text-align: justify;margin-top:12pt;margin-bottom:12pt;\"><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 12px; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\">If these problems suddenly occur, call or contact the nearest Authorized Dealer for a rescue. Lucky Lion provide free Rescue and/or Service for our customer.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.38; text-indent: 36pt; text-align: center; margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 12pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; font-style: italic; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">Tips:</span><span style=\"font-size: 12px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"> for the better E-bike experience:&nbsp; have your unit regularly check. It’s either at home or by visiting Lucky Lion Stores</span><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">.</span></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 8pt; font-family: Nunito, sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><br/></span></p><p><br/></p>"
      },
      {
        "id": "brakes-tires",
        "title": "How to check your Brakes and Tires?",
        "html": "<p><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(21, 31, 109); font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\">How to check your Brakes and Tires?</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: rgb(21, 31, 109); font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"><br/></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: rgb(21, 31, 109); font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\">CHECKING BRAKE : STEP - BY - STEP</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: Nunito, sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">BRAKE</span><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: Nunito, sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"> (there are 2 ways to check your Ebike&#39;s brake)</span></span></p><p><br/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: Nunito, sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">First, ride and brake: </span><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: Nunito, sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">hop on ebike and throttle drive then press the brake, repeat 3 times. if it stops upon pressing then your ebike&#39;s brake is in good condition.</span></span></p><p><br/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: Nunito, sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">second brake press :</span><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-family: Nunito, sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"> press the brake both left and right, if it reach the handle, call or visit nearest Lucky Lion Authorized dealer for service</span></span></p><p><br/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: rgb(255, 255, 255); background-color: rgb(21, 31, 109); font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\">CHECKING TIRES : STEP - BY - STEP</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><br/></p><ol style=\"padding-inline-start: 48px;\" class=\" list-paddingleft-2\"><li><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap: wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\">Park to the Bright area and use the center stand to clearly see the Tires</span></p></li><li><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap: wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\">Using hand Pinch the tires if soft&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap: wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\">Check if there are nails or sharp objects.</span></p></li><li><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap: wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\">if tires are not soft and no sharp object you are ready to go</span></p></li><li><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap: wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\">they are soft and/or have sharp Object that cause holes call the nearest Lucky Lion Authorized dealers for service / if stuck on the road the customer are can call for Rescue</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap: wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"></span></p></li></ol><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap: wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap: wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"><br/></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap: wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height: 1.38; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap: wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 9pt; font-weight: 400; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap: wrap; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"></span></p><p><br/></p><p><br/></p>"
      },
      {
        "id": "charger-blink",
        "title": "Charger Blinking RED & GREEN what to do?",
        "html": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\"><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 107%;\">Check first the battery voltage if not below 40v, if below 40v much better call for home service to check the battery to test in battery machine.</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px; line-height: 107%;\"></span></span></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"\"></span><img src=\"assets/maintenance/charger-blink-0.jpg\" style=\"width: 504px;\"/><span style=\"\"></span></p>"
      },
      {
        "id": "footbrake-erv",
        "title": "When use foot brake Ebike Stop? (foot-brake units)",
        "html": "<p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; text-indent: 0in; line-height: normal; text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei';\">1. <span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">Step on the foot brake then check if the foot brake goes up to the same position before you step on it.</span></span></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"assets/maintenance/footbrake-erv-1.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"width: 248px;\"/><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-size: 12px;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span><img src=\"assets/maintenance/footbrake-erv-2.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"width: 250px;\"/></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-size: 12px;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12px; font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal;\">***</span><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 9px; line-height: normal;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-size: 13px;\">IF NOT GO BACK ASK FOR HOME SERVICE</span></span></p><p><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-size: 12px;\"></span></p><p style=\";margin-bottom:0;text-indent:0in;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-size: 12px;\">2. IF THE FOOT BRAKE GOES BACK</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:56px\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-size: 12px;\">a)<span style=\"font: 9px &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Do not turn off the e-bike go at the back of the bike and check the brake lights if it was turn on.</span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left: 56px; text-align: center;\"><img src=\"assets/maintenance/footbrake-erv-3.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"width: 308px;\"/></p><p style=\";margin-left:56px;margin-bottom:0;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-size: 12px;\">b)<span style=\"font: 9px &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>If it was off bus still not move call the nearest branch for home service</span></p><p><br/></p><p style=\";margin-bottom:0;text-indent:0in;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-size: 12px;\">3. <span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-size: 13px;\">IF THE LIGHT ARE ON</span></span></p><p style=\";margin-left:56px;margin-bottom:0;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-size: 12px;\">a)<span style=\"font: 9px &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>Below the foot brake there is a switch remove it and see if the brake light will turn off.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-size: 12px;\"><br/></span><img src=\"assets/maintenance/footbrake-erv-4.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"width: 376px;\"/></p><p><span style=\"font-family: 'Microsoft YaHei'; font-size: 12px;\">4. IF IT WORK OR STILL IT, BRING THE UNIT TO THE NEAREST STORE TO CHECK OR ASK FOR SERVICE FOR YOUR SAFETY</span></p><p><br/></p>"
      },
      {
        "id": "adjust-seat-erv",
        "title": "How to adjust seat of Ebike?",
        "html": "<p style=\"text-align:center\"><strong><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%\">HOW TO ADJUST SEAT OF EBIKE?</span></strong></p><p><br/></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%\">1.&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%;font-family:&#39;Calibri&#39;,sans-serif\">Look for this lever under the seat front part.</span></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%;font-family:&#39;Calibri&#39;,sans-serif\"><img src=\"assets/maintenance/adjust-seat-erv-1000.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"width: 231px;\"/></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%;font-family:&#39;Calibri&#39;,sans-serif\"><br/></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%;font-family:&#39;Calibri&#39;,sans-serif\"><br/></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><br/></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%;font-family:&#39;Calibri&#39;,sans-serif\"></span></span></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\">2. Push it to the right then move the seat forward then.</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"assets/maintenance/adjust-seat-erv-1001.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"width: 325px;\"/></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\">3. Pull the back part of the seat forward with force and it will release to go down.</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"assets/maintenance/adjust-seat-erv-1002.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"width: 290px;\"/>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<img src=\"assets/maintenance/adjust-seat-erv-1003.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"width: 303px;\"/></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%;font-family:&#39;Calibri&#39;,sans-serif\"></span></span><br/></p>"
      },
      {
        "id": "disc-brake-loose",
        "title": "What to do if Disc brake is weak/loose?  (models with disc brakes)",
        "html": "<p><span style=\"font-size:14px;line-height:107%\">Having Problem in your disc brake? Check this simple troubleshoot to check if your e-bike is can fix in a simple way or you may need to the nearest branches to check and fix your disc brake problem.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: normal; font-size: 14px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 9px; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;</span>CHECK IF IT HAVE FLUID - brake fluid helps transfer the movement and force created when you press down on the brake pedal.</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:52px\"><br/></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left: 52px; text-align: center;\"><img src=\"assets/maintenance/disc-brake-loose-1004.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"width: 190px;\"/></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left: 52px;\">2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 9px; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>IF IT IS CLEAR OPEN THE COVER AND CHECK.</p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left: 52px;\"><br/></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left: 52px; text-align: center;\"><img src=\"assets/maintenance/disc-brake-loose-1005.png\" alt=\"\"/></p><p style=\"text-indent:28px\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;3. NOTE USE ONLY BRAKE FLUID AND DO NOT OVER FILL.</p><p style=\"text-indent: 28px; text-align: center;\"><img src=\"assets/maintenance/disc-brake-loose-1006.png\" alt=\"\"/></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:52px\"><br/></p><p style=\"margin-left:28px\"><strong>IF STILL THE BRAKE IS LOOSE CALL THE NEAREST BRANCH AND ASK FOR HOME SERVICE FOR SAFETY.</strong></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:52px\"><br/></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:52px\"><br/></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:52px\"><br/></p><p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left:52px\"><br/></p>"
      },
      {
        "id": "remote-function",
        "title": "Lucky Lion Guide 101: Essential Functions of Your Lucky Lion Remote",
        "html": "<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-indent: 36pt;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Understanding the various functions and features of your Lucky Lion vehicle is crucial for ensuring a convenient and comfortable driving experience. This guide is designed to help every user effectively utilize their remote.</span></p><p><br/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Here’s a simple overview of the remote&#39;s key functions:</span></p><p><br/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">1. Lock Key</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- To secure your vehicle, gently press the lock symbol “🔒”.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Activating this function also enables the anti-theft device/alarm for enhanced security.</span></p><p><br/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">2. Unlock Key</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- To gain access to your vehicle, press the unlock symbol “🔓”.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- This action deactivates the alarm or anti-theft device, allowing for safe usage.</span></p><p><br/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">3. Start Button</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- To power up or start your e-bike, press the thunder symbol “⚡️” twice.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- This feature allows you to operate the vehicle without using a key, entering a remote start state.</span></p><p><br/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">4. Bell Button</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Press the bell icon “🔔” to locate your vehicle.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Activating this function prompts your vehicle to respond with a sound, helping you find it easily.</span></p><p><br/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\">Important Note:</span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"> Lucky Lion electric vehicles are equipped with an anti-theft alarm system. If the vehicle is locked and is moved by an external force, the lights will flash, and a continuous alarm will sound. To silence or turn off the alarm, simply press the unlock symbol.</span></span></p><p><br/></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.2;text-indent: 36pt;text-align: justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">By familiarizing yourself with the functions of your remote and vehicle, you can maximize the advantages of its features. Remember to drive safely and smartly. For additional tips and guides, visit our social media pages and website.</span></p><div><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Century Gothic', sans-serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><br/></span></div><p><br/></p>"
      },
      {
        "id": "reverse-not-work",
        "title": "WHAT TO DO IF MY EBIKE REVERSE DON’T WORK",
        "html": "<p>1.&nbsp;TURN ON THE UNIT THEN PRESS THE SWITCH TO REVERSE</p><p>2.&nbsp;SLOWLY TURN THE TROTTLE AND CHECK IF IT WILL MOVE REVERSE</p><p><img src=\"assets/maintenance/reverse-not-work-1007.png\" style=\"width: 200px; margin: 0px; border: 0px solid;\" width=\"200\" height=\"290\" border=\"0\" hspace=\"0\" vspace=\"0\" title=\"\"/><img src=\"assets/maintenance/reverse-not-work-1008.png\" width=\"157\" height=\"290\" border=\"0\" hspace=\"0\" vspace=\"0\" title=\"\" style=\"width: 157px; margin: 0px; border: 0px solid;\"/></p><p>D - FORWARD O - FORWARD</p><p>R - BACKWARD - &nbsp;&nbsp;- BACKWARD</p><p>3.IF STILL NOT WORKING CALL FOR HOME SERVICE OR VISIT NEAREST BRANCH</p><p>4.POSSIBLE PROBLEM COMBINATION SWITCH</p><p><br/></p>"
      },
      {
        "id": "handbrake-stuck",
        "title": "WHAT TO DO IF MY HANDBRAKE IS NOT RETURNING UP AFTER PRESSING?",
        "html": "<p>1.&nbsp;CHECK THE SPRING IF STILL OK OR HAVE<br/>2.&nbsp;IF BROKEN ASK FOR SERVICE DON’T BRING IN OFFICE<br/><img src=\"assets/maintenance/handbrake-stuck-1009.png\" width=\"183\" height=\"300\" border=\"0\" hspace=\"0\" vspace=\"0\" title=\"\" style=\"width: 183px; margin: 0px; border: 0px solid;\"/><br/>3.CHECK THE SPRING ON THE BRAKE CABLE IF HAVE PULL TO MAKE IT LONGER<br/>4.&nbsp;IF DON’T HAVE ASK BRANCH TO DO HOME SERVICE<br/><img src=\"assets/maintenance/handbrake-stuck-1010.png\" width=\"500\" height=\"231\" border=\"0\" hspace=\"0\" vspace=\"0\" title=\"\" style=\"width: 500px; margin: 0px; border: 0px solid;\"/><br/>5.POSSIBLE PROBLEM BRAKE HANDLE, BRAKE CABLE OR BRAKE HUB COVER<br/>6. IF BRAKE IS THE PROBLE BETTER TO ASK FOR HOME SERVICE FOR SAFETY ISSUE<br/><span style=\"font-family: Calibri; font-size: medium;\">&nbsp;</span><br/></p><blockquote style=\"margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;\"><blockquote style=\"margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;\"><p><br/></p></blockquote></blockquote>"
      },
      {
        "id": "wont-turn-off",
        "title": "WHAT TO DO IF MY EBIKE WON’T TURN OFF?",
        "html": "<blockquote style=\"margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;\"></blockquote><p><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em;\">1.Check the unlock sign in the remove.</span><br/></p><blockquote style=\"margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;\"></blockquote><p><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em;\">Because alarm system can on unit without key.If it didn&#39;t turn off ,Follow step 2.</span><br/></p><blockquote style=\"margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;\"></blockquote><p><img src=\"assets/maintenance/wont-turn-off-1011.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"345\" border=\"0\" hspace=\"0\" vspace=\"0\" title=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em; margin: 0px; border-style: solid;\"/><br/></p><blockquote style=\"margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;\"></blockquote><p><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em;\">2. Remove the connection of the battery or turn off using the switch inside the seat compartment.</span><br/></p><blockquote style=\"margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;\"></blockquote><p><img src=\"assets/maintenance/wont-turn-off-1012.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"131\" border=\"0\" hspace=\"0\" vspace=\"0\" title=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em; margin: 0px; border-style: solid;\"/><br/></p><blockquote style=\"margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;\"></blockquote><p><img src=\"assets/maintenance/wont-turn-off-1013.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"333\" border=\"0\" hspace=\"0\" vspace=\"0\" title=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em; margin: 0px; border-style: solid;\"/><br/></p><blockquote style=\"margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;\"></blockquote><p><img src=\"assets/maintenance/wont-turn-off-1014.png\" width=\"200\" height=\"215\" border=\"0\" hspace=\"0\" vspace=\"0\" title=\"\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em; margin: 0px; border-style: solid;\"/><br/></p><blockquote style=\"margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;\"></blockquote><p><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em;\">3.Check if the ebike turn off, then put back the plug or turn on the switch.</span><br/></p><blockquote style=\"margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;\"></blockquote><p><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em;\">If still the ebike turn on, call to the nearest branch for home service or bring to the nearest store.</span><br/></p><blockquote style=\"margin: 0 0 0 40px; border: none; padding: 0px;\"></blockquote><p><span style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em;\">Posisble problem is alarm system for unit with remote or key swicth.</span><br/></p><p style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em;\">Reminders never let your unit somewhere, because it was turn on!!!</p><p><br/></p><p style=\"margin: 0 0 0;font-family: Calibri;font-size: medium;text-indent: 0;white-space: normal\"><br/></p>"
      }
    ]
  },
